# What must NOT enter the build context.
#
# ⚠ A BARE PATTERN IS ROOT-ONLY. Docker matches each line against the whole path from the context
# root, and `*` does not cross `/` — so `.pytest_cache` excludes exactly `./.pytest_cache` and says
# nothing about `src/mantle/.pytest_cache/`. That one is not academic: `build/Dockerfile` does
# `COPY src/mantle/ ./mantle/`, so a pytest cache under `src/mantle/` is copied INTO THE RUNTIME
# IMAGE. Anything meant to apply at any depth carries `**/`; the entries below that do not are
# root-only on purpose (`.git`, `src/*.egg-info`).

.git
.gitignore
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache
src/*.egg-info
.coverage

# ⭐ THE DEV KEYSET LIVES HERE, SO THIS LINE IS ABOUT SECRETS, NOT SIZE. `docker-compose.yml`
# tells an operator to run `dev_init_keys.py --keys-dir ./.data/keys` before `up --build`, which
# puts `encryption.key` and `mantle.private.pem` directly in the context of the very next build.
# Nothing in the Dockerfile copies them — but a build context is uploaded to the daemon whole, and
# private key material should not be in it. `.data/` is a runtime volume root; none of it is input
# to a build.
.data/
.data-*/

# A real `.env` is a developer's own secrets. `.env.example` is the template and is documentation,
# so it is deliberately not matched here.
.env

# The store, its sidecars, and the embeddings cache — runtime state at any depth, never build
# input. `.data/mantle-lattice.db` is where the default puts one and `.data/mantle/mantle.db` is
# where the compose flow does, but MANTLE_LATTICE_PATH can name any depth, so these are unanchored.
**/*.db
**/*.db-shm
**/*.db-wal
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite-shm
**/*.sqlite-wal
